WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.567
Florida governor

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.534
Ron DeSantis,

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.569
who is an expected

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.738
20, 24 presidential hopeful,

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.539
is breaking his silence on Trump's

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.273
legal troubles

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.775
and the looming indictment.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:09.542
DeSantis calling

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.010
the Manhattan

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.378
District Attorney's investigation

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.812
politically motivated

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.279
and vowing

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.781
that his office won't get involved

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.316
if the matter reaches his state,

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.251
though it's not expected to.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.586
At the same time, though,

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.954
he made a point of highlighting

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.022
the conduct

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:25.725
at the heart of the investigation

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.660
I don't know what goes into

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.763
paying hush money to a porn star

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.231
to to secure silence

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.266
over some type of alleged affair.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.069
I just I can't speak to that

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.405
but what I can speak to

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.640
is that if you have a prosecutor

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.411
who is ignoring crimes happening

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.280
every single day in his jurisdiction,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.848
and he chooses to go back

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.850
many, many years ago

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.520
to try to use something about

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.256
porn star hush money payments,

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.857
you know, that's an example

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:58.591
of pursuing

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.226
a political agenda

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.662
and weaponizing the office.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.063
So, you know,

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.730
he was getting asked

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.131
that question by a reporter,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.933
but he had been facing

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.501
some pressure from Trump's allies.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.170
Why haven't you said anything about this?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.971
Because we saw a lot of other Republicans

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.673
weighing in as soon as on Saturday.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.475
And DeSantis in Orlando yesterday.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.709
But but notable, you know,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.411
he got criticized by Donald Trump Jr

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.979
who said he thought he was minimizing it.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.414
And his response

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.649
is a little shady, right.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.017
When he didn't have to point out.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.985
Did not have to point the heart of this?

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:26.686
The obvious.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.520
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.488
Well, House Republicans

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.690
trying to intervene to defend,

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.692
you know, head of this Donald Trump,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.860
a possible indictment here of House

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.561
Judiciary Chairman

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.462
Jim Jordan

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.663
and two other committee chairs

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.331
are demanding testimony

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.699
from Manhattan's justice attorney.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.834
It's an extraordinary move

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.635
because Alvin Bragg doesn't work

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.636
for the federal government.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.105
He's a local prosecutor

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.973
and this isn't a federal case.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:47.640
In a letter,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.776
the chairman accuse Bragg

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.612
of unprecedented abuse of prosecute

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.481
prosecutors moral authority.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.081
Congressman Jim

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.349
Jordan admits that he doesn't

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.183
actually know the full

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.585
scope of potential charges.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.054
But you don't know

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.022
the charges against him

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.524
on what you guys have told us.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.926
That's all been jumping to conclusions

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.294
because he may have broken the law

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.496
as a concern.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.263
We don't think

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:10.730
and we don't think

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.532
President Trump broke the law at all.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.466
But what concerns me

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.368
is what they're going to do based on

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.470
what's been reported by Southwest.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.238
Yeah, it's interesting

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.506
that they're making all of these comments

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.373
and they don't even know

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.107
what's going to happen

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.442
if there's even going to be

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.042
an indictment.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.544
So that's why we turn to CNN's

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.412
Melanie's are known to live in Orlando

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:27.447
where House Republicans

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.482
are having their annual retreat.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.850
So I'm sure she's got information

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.184
on that.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.218
Good morning to you, Melanie.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.720
What's the latest

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.289
Good morning to you, Don,

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.891
from chilly Orlando.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.058
But House Republicans

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.094
are turning up the heat on the Manhattan

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.095
district attorney's office

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.364
ahead of a possible Trump indictment.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.065
Three committee chairmen yesterday

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.134
fired off a letter to Alvin Bragg.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.669
They are seeking both documents

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.305
and his testimony by March.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.306
23rd.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.107
They want to know

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.808
whether federal funds were used

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.676
to investigate

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.077
Donald Trump over this hush money

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.913
payment to Stormy Daniels.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.080
And they also want to know

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.815
whether there was any communication

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.983
between the Manhattan D.A.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:04.751
office

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.753
and between the Department of Justice.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.087
I want to read you part of the letter

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:08.688
where they explained

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.822
some of their reasoning.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.824
They wrote, Your decision to pursue

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.525
such a

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.494
politically motivated prosecution

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.028
that requires

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.329
congressional scrutiny

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.131
about how public safety funds

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.832
appropriated by Congress

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.733
are implemented

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.969
by local law enforcement agencies.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.571
Now, Republicans admit

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.005
they don't have any knowledge

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.040
of whether federal funds

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.408
are actually used

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.143
in these sorts of cases.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.077
And they also admit

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:31.711
they don't know

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.680
the full scope of the charges

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.281
that Trump might be facing.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.749
So it really shows

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.685
the extraordinary lengths

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:39.085
that House

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.920
Republicans are willing to go

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.955
to defend Trump

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.022
and to try to discredit

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.890
this investigation.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.526
Is pressing brag

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.761
something the entire GOP agrees on here?

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.263
I mean, could they be jumping the gun

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:50.964
since they don't know?

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:51.664
As I said,

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.365
they don't know

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.866
if charges will even be filed.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:54.834
Melanie

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.404
Right, Don, we've actually been asking

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.105
that request,

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.740
that exact question to Republicans

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.342
here at their policy retreat.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:02.775
So far,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.611
I've only talked to one Republican,

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.245
Don Bacon,

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.846
who represents a Biden district

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.747
who said it would be more

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.249
appropriate to wait

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.451
until they see the actual indictment.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.485
But most Republicans

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:13.753
are defending this effort

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.822
to intervene in an ongoing

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:16.489
criminal probe.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.724
Again, a very extraordinary

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.459
and unprecedented move.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.994
Speaker Kevin McCarthy in a pen

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.228
and pad with reporters yesterday

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.497
said they have a right to ask questions.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.199
Scott Perry, the chairman of the House

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.066
Freedom Caucus, told me

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:27.834
they don't need to wait

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:28.835
because they see the writing

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.236
on the wall here.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:30.970
But Democrats

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.739
see this as an abuse of power,

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.841
a waste of congressional resources

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:35.842
and the Manhattan

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:36.876
District Attorney's Office

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.411
said they will not be intimidated

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.912
by any effort to interfere

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.180
in the justice system. Don.

